{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1488167-question-about-access-to-devotions-and-bloodline-devotions","id":1488167,"title":"Question about access to Devotions and Bloodline Devotions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-27T07:05:05-07:00","id":1488167,"title":"Question about access to Devotions and Bloodline Devotions","content":"Hello<br /> <br /> After reading in-depth Vampire and some supplements, there is something I don't understand: How exclusive Devotions work?<br /> <br /> I mean, Devotions are tricks pulled by cleverly and sometimes symbolic combination or deepening of Disciplines. This is something that theorically any Kindred who have the prerrequisites can even do without a teacher (but with a teacher is easy). How can a Bloodline then have <i>exclusive</i> Devotions? No Kindred can have the same idea and combination without being part of the Bloodline? It seems weird by how I feel Devotions are defined, anyone with enough dedication can have that Devotions, not only Bloodline members, so it seems like a &quot;wasted&quot; Bloodline Gift. There is something I'm not understanding about Devotions?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance for any answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27384-altidiya","name":"altidiya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T08:35:16-07:00","id":1488171,"title":"","content":"Because Devotions and other magic don't work purely on being able to conceive of an idea for a supernatural power and because bloodlines are groups with secrets and good reason to keep them. Same reason demons bother reverse-engineering gadgets found in Infrastructure to learn new Embeds. Same reason Beasts need Family Ties with a monster to develop new Kinship Nightmares. Same reason mages need Mastery of an Arcanum and a not-insignificant amount of time to codify a new Rote.<br /> <br /> The way the supernatural works in this setting, you're typically going to need some kernel of experiential focus to actually get results rather than relying on imagination alone and smushing concepts together. &quot;Theoretically possible&quot; doesn't translate to &quot;narratively practical.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T08:50:41-07:00","id":1488173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1488167-question-about-access-to-devotions-and-bloodline-devotions?p=1488171#post1488171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because Devotions and other magic don't work purely on being able to conceive of an idea for a supernatural power and because bloodlines are groups with secrets and good reason to keep them. Same reason demons bother reverse-engineering gadgets found in Infrastructure to learn new Embeds. Same reason Beasts need Family Ties with a monster to develop new Kinship Nightmares. Same reason mages need Mastery of an Arcanum and a not-insignificant amount of time to codify a new Rote.<br /> <br /> The way the supernatural works in this setting, you're typically going to need some kernel of experiential focus to actually get results rather than relying on imagination alone and smushing concepts together. &quot;Theoretically possible&quot; doesn't translate to &quot;narratively practical.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I understand that, but in that examples this are not restricted. In the way that any Demon can reverse-engineering gadgets, any Beast can create Famility Ties and any Mage can codify a Rote when they have the mastery and the time. I don't have problem with the narrative aspects of the learning process, I'm not defending &quot;a Vampire can create a Devotion at the speed of though&quot;, my problem is more with the word &quot;exclusive&quot; on this Devotions.<br /> <br /> If any vampire can have them by learning from a source or developt <i>mechanical equal</i> Devotions with enough time and dedication, then the Devotion is not &quot;exclusive&quot; for me, and seems like a wasted gift. Bloodlines can have favored Devotions, that sounds right, but giving as a gift a Devotion that any vampire with the same Disciplines could -with enough dedication- replicate seems a little off. The other options is that this Devotions aren't capable of being created without the Bloodline, but Devotion don't seem to have that level of restriction as Disciplines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27384-altidiya","name":"altidiya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T09:41:37-07:00","id":1488179,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s built in to the bloodline, unique to them. You need to be able to join that bloodline to learn them, because those Devotions are expressions of that unique lineage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T10:32:07-07:00","id":1488185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>altidiya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1488167-question-about-access-to-devotions-and-bloodline-devotions?p=1488173#post1488173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If any vampire can have them by learning from a source or developt <i>mechanical equal</i> Devotions with enough time and dedication, then the Devotion is not &quot;exclusive&quot; for me, and seems like a wasted gift.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry to hear that, but when the corebook says that Devotions are rare enough to have intrinsic value as secrets and usually require a teacher, that's limited enough to be reasonably called &quot;exclusive&quot; for a group as particular and theoretically-okay-with-murder as a vampire bloodline, regardless of your perspective on the semantics of the term.<br /> <br /> You already need a donor to develop half the common Disciplines that exist out-of-clan and bloodlines universally get an extra Discipline affinity along with their other benefits. Basic practices of secrecy in the vein of not showing off proprietary powers outside of your own subculture are already ingrained in the magically-oriented covenants' control of their Coils and sorceries \u2014 it's not unreasonable to conclude that bloodlines' exclusive Devotions are kept private enough that whatever principles of the Blood make them work aren't going to be stumbled upon by a random neonate beating their head against the wall for ten years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-28T15:42:15-07:00","id":1488287,"title":"","content":"For my 2 cents, it seems to be an Egg of Columbus matter. The \u2018recipe\u2019 is simple enough that an out-of-bloodline vampire could try to replicate it\u2026 if they only had the right tilt of perspective to kickstart that innovation. But they rarely do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T23:23:25-07:00","id":1489841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1488167-question-about-access-to-devotions-and-bloodline-devotions?p=1488287#post1488287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For my 2 cents, it seems to be an Egg of Columbus matter. The \u2018recipe\u2019 is simple enough that an out-of-bloodline vampire could try to replicate it\u2026 if they only had the right tilt of perspective to kickstart that innovation. But they rarely do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you forgotten when the game talks about whether a given devotion or rite even could be learned by others? There are cases where the prerequisites for developing a power explicitly says that a vampire must be of a particular Bloodline. I believe there was even a case where one bloodline could not teach their blood sorcery rites to others, while another could but required those vampires as teachers every time the rites are taught to outsiders. <br /> <br /> Truth be told, I don't really know the answer myself, but near the beginning of the 2nd edition I came up with a theory. Altidiya, have you ever considered that maybe the bloodline devotions are not completely covered by the typical disciplines? Think about it: the disciplines are only so flexible, so they require other discipline components to stretch even farther. Yet sometimes it is not enough. My headcanon is that the &quot;stillborn&quot; bloodline discipline still became &quot;potential&quot;: not a complete power by itself but could be combined with the existing disciplines to achieve discrete and unique abilities. Obviously this is not every case. Just innovating devotions for your bloodline doesn't mean it incorporates your special potential. Though sometimes it cheapens development. <br /> <br /> Got a better theory?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T23:34:58-07:00","id":1489842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1488167-question-about-access-to-devotions-and-bloodline-devotions?p=1489841#post1489841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Have you forgotten when the game talks about whether a given devotion or rite even could be learned by others? There are cases where the prerequisites for developing a power explicitly says that a vampire must be of a particular Bloodline. I believe there was even a case where one bloodline could not teach their blood sorcery rites to others, while another could but required those vampires as teachers every time the rites are taught to outsiders. </div> </div> </div> </div>If it has that much of a restriction described, as opposed to just a simple word of \u2018It\u2019s exclusive\u2019, then yes I suppose it\u2019s truly restricted. But I thought the topic was about \u2018grey area\u2019 ones here?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}